      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In experiments on anesthetized cats and dogs it was shown that the anti-ischemic action of verapamil and diltiazem injected intravenously in acute permanent occlusion of the coronary artery is not related to their effect on the collateral blood supply to the myocardial ischemic focus. The protective effect of the drugs in this case is due to other mechanisms one of which is a decrease of oxygen consumption by the heart."},
